From aca1e613f76820109f432457dfb9bcd714c8bca1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "exe.dev user" <exedev@erbium-qemu.exe.xyz>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 23:13:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] sw-sysemu(erbium): file-backed MRAM region and SCCR stub

* memory/mmap_region.h: MmapRegion<Base,N>, a MemoryRegion backed by a
  MAP_SHARED mapping of a file (created/grown to N if needed, never
  truncated so contents survive MainMemory::reset()). No reset pattern:
  it exposes the file contents like non-volatile memory.
* MainMemory::mram_file: when set, MRAM is an MmapRegion instead of a
  DenseRegion. The old mapping is dropped before re-mapping on reset.
* devices/sccr_er.h: SccrEr stub for the xSPI SCCR block at
  ERBIUM_TOP_XSPI_REGISTERS_BASE (0x40 bytes, 64-bit stride, reset
  ID0=0x2 CFG=0x1382) so minion firmware touching it does not fault.
  Real SCCR behaviour lives on the host (QEMU) side.
* MainMemory::access_sizes(): tells host-side agents what access sizes a
  region accepts (needed to split arbitrary host accesses).
* MainMemory::por_reset(): reset sysregs (cause POR) and SCCR without
  touching memory contents; SysregsEr::reset() made public for that.

Co-authored-by: Shelley <shelley@exe.dev>
